        role: "Insurance adjuster",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job.", "\"I'm an insurance adjuster. I investigate property claims after fires and other losses and compare what customers claim with what the records show.\""), .direct("How did {D}'s claim come to your attention?", "\"The claim totaled $18,000 in belongings, which was high for the size of the home, so I did a standard review of the inventory.\""), .direct("What did you find when you checked the inventory?", "\"Several of the items had been sold months earlier on online listings. I found sale records for a television, tools and a set of furniture.\""), .direct("How did you confirm the sales?", "\"Through the listing pages and buyer messages, which showed the item, the price and the sale date.\""), .direct("What did the claim form ask the customer to certify?", "\"It asks the customer to certify that the list is a true and complete account of items owned at the time of the loss.\""), .direct("What was the fire's effect on the home?", "\"There was real damage in the kitchen and living room. I don't dispute that a fire occurred and that some belongings were lost.\""), .cross("Did the claim form come with a pre-filled template?", "\"Our online portal offers a template with common household items, yes. A customer can edit it.\""), .cross("Could the template have included items from an earlier claim?", "\"It's possible in principle, but I can't say it happened here without checking.\""), .cross("Did {DL} cooperate when you called about the discrepancies?", "\"Yes, {D.he} returned my calls and said the list was from memory.\""), .cross("Did {DL} lose real belongings in the fire?", "\"Yes, there were real losses. The question is only about certain entries.\""), .cross("Was the total claim paid out?", "\"No. The claim was held pending review, and nothing was paid on the disputed items.\"")],
