        truths: ("{DL} advertised the claimed items online before the fire, and sale records show they were sold.", "The adjuster's template pulled in items from a prior claim by mistake, so some entries were not {DL}'s own list."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you submit a claim for $18,000 in belongings?", "\"Yes, I did. I filed it a few days after the fire, while I was staying with my sister.\""), .direct("How did you prepare the list?", "\"From memory, with the insurer's online form open on a borrowed laptop. I was tired and stressed, and I clicked through quickly.\""), .direct("Did you know some of those items had been sold?", "\"I knew I'd sold a few things in the spring. I did not realize they were on my list.\""), .direct("Why were they on the list?", "\"The form had a pre-filled list of items from a prior claim, and I think I left some entries without checking.\""), .direct("What did you lose in the fire?", "\"A lot. The kitchen, most of the living room, my clothes, and things my kids had kept in their rooms.\""), .direct("What did you do when the adjuster called?", "\"I told him the list was from memory and that I would fix any mistakes. I offered to send receipts.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, I have, and I know how that looks next to an inflated claim. I didn't mean to cheat anyone.\""), .cross("You certified that the list was complete and true, didn't you?", "\"I checked the box, yes. I didn't read it as carefully as I should have.\""), .cross("You advertised those items online yourself, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did. I forgot they were still on the list when I filled it in.\""), .cross("Nobody forced you to file a claim for $18,000, did they?", "\"No. I chose the amount, and I take responsibility for it.\""), .cross("You haven't corrected the claim yet, have you?", "\"Not yet. I was told to wait until this case was over, and I'll fix it right away.\"")],
